<title>USA: No indication of govt action on oil stocks - analyst.</title>
<headline>No indication of govt action on oil stocks - analyst.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>There was no indication of any government action on heating oil stocks at a meeting Friday between Energy Secretary Hazel O'Leary and industry representatives, a participant at the meeting said.</p>
<p>&quot;There was no indication the government intends to do anything,&quot; analyst John Lichtblau of the Petroleum Industry Research Foundation told reporters after the meeting.</p>
<p>He said the Strategic Petroleum Reserve was discussed in the meeting but there was no move to release any of it.</p>
</text>
